      <Placemark>
        <name>Khirbet Jarassur (ח&apos;רבת ג&apos;אראסור)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Jarassur (ח&apos;רבת ג&apos;אראסור)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 02. Pre-Pottery Neolithic (PPN) (-8300 to -5500 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Mesopotamia</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.2 (Pages 45)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (02. Pre-Pottery Neolithic):</b></p>
<p>A well, briefly reported from Northern Iraq, without detailed information, dimensions, or drawings. It was considered the oldest well in the world by some researchers before the discovery at Atlit-Yam.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Pre_Pottery_Neolithic</styleUrl>
