    <Folder>
      <name>04. Chalcolithic Period (-4500 to -3300 BCE)</name>
      <description>התקופה הכלקוליתית - 5 sites</description>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Abu Huf (אבו חוף)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Abu Huf (אבו חוף)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 04. Chalcolithic Period (-4500 to -3300 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.4.1 (Pages 52, 54)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (04. Chalcolithic Period):</b></p>
<p>A round well, 1.5-1.55m in inner diameter and 2.45m deep, constructed of dry-laid fieldstones. It was dug into gravel alluvium next to a wadi channel and was associated with a building and courtyard.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Chalcolithic</styleUrl>
