        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Horbat Beter (חורבת בתר)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Horbat Beter (חורבת בתר)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 04. Chalcolithic Period (-4500 to -3300 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.4.2 (Pages 52, 54)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (04. Chalcolithic Period):</b></p>
<p>A cylindrical well, 2m in diameter and 3m deep, excavated into loess soil down to the ancient streambed of Nahal Beersheba. Two steps were cut into its upper walls, and it was intentionally filled at a later stage.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Chalcolithic</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Horbat Beter</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>חורבת בתר</value></Data>
