      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Rajajil (ראג&apos;אג&apos;יל (ערב הסעודית))</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Rajajil (ראג&apos;אג&apos;יל (ערב הסעודית))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 04. Chalcolithic Period (-4500 to -3300 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Saudi Arabia</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.4.4 (Pages 53, 54)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (04. Chalcolithic Period):</b></p>
<p>An abandoned well, located about 1 km west of the megalithic complex, characterized by small stones, troughs, and rope marks. Its Chalcolithic dating is suggested but not definitively confirmed without excavation.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Chalcolithic</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Rajajil</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>ראג&apos;אג&apos;יל (ערב הסעודית)</value></Data>
