        <Point>
          <coordinates>39.904,29.809,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tepe Gawra (טפה גאורה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tepe Gawra (טפה גאורה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 04. Chalcolithic Period (-4500 to -3300 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Mesopotamia</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.4.3 (Pages 53, 54)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (04. Chalcolithic Period):</b></p>
<p>An Ubaid period well, 1.15m in diameter at its rim, excavated to a depth of 12-13m. It was found a few centimeters below the holy of holies floor of the northern temple of Layer XIII, and its water was used by the city&apos;s acropolis.</p>]]></description>
