    <Folder>
      <name>05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</name>
      <description>תקופת הברונזה הקדומה (EB I-IV) - 19 sites</description>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Ai (et-Tell) (העי (א-תל))</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Ai (et-Tell) (העי (א-תל))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.10, 2.5 (Pages 59, 71)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A large open-air reservoir in Area K, exceeding 1800 cubic meters in volume, 25m wide, and 2.5m deep. It was designed to collect runoff water from the upper city via channels, featuring a stone floor on clay and a thick dam wall, dating to EB 1-3. The only known instance of plaster from this period is from a water pool at Ai, where impermeable clayey soil was used as a hydraulic material to line the reservoir.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Early_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Ai (et-Tell)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>העי (א-תל)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Era"><value>05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Water Reservoir</value></Data>
          <Data name="Region"><value>Judean Hills</value></Data>
          <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dates"><value>-3300 to -2200 BCE</value></Data>
          <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.5.10, 2.5</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>59, 71</value></Data>
          <Data name="Description"><value>A large open-air reservoir in Area K, exceeding 1800 cubic meters in volume, 25m wide, and 2.5m deep. It was designed to collect runoff water from the upper city via channels, featuring a stone floor on clay and a thick dam wall, dating to EB 1-3. The only known instance of plaster from this period is from a water pool at Ai, where impermeable clayey soil was used as a hydraulic material to line the reservoir.</value></Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>35.2611,31.9167,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Barqa (ברקת)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Barqa (ברקת)</h3>
