      <Placemark>
        <name>Mezer (מצר)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Mezer (מצר)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.15 (Pages 68)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Multiple rock-cut cisterns, including a large one (B3) 5m deep and another (D7) with niches, were used for rainwater collection via rock-cut channels. These cisterns were unplastered due to the impermeable Nari and chalk bedrock.</p>]]></description>
