      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Dalit (תל דלית)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Dalit (תל דלית)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.16 (Pages 68, 69, 70)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A fortified Early Bronze Age settlement with several rock-cut cisterns in soft chalk bedrock, designed to collect rainwater. One examined cistern was irregular, 2.2m deep to the chamber, with a rectangular chamber 2.6x2.0m, showing no signs of plaster due to the impermeable chalk. Shallow wells in nearby wadis likely supplemented water supply during peacetime.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Early_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Dalit</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>תל דלית</value></Data>
          <Data name="Era"><value>05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Deep Well</value></Data>
          <Data name="Region"><value>Judean Hills</value></Data>
          <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dates"><value>-3300 to -2200 BCE</value></Data>
          <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.5.16</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>68, 69, 70</value></Data>
          <Data name="Description"><value>A fortified Early Bronze Age settlement with several rock-cut cisterns in soft chalk bedrock, designed to collect rainwater. One examined cistern was irregular, 2.2m deep to the chamber, with a rectangular chamber 2.6x2.0m, showing no signs of plaster due to the impermeable chalk. Shallow wells in nearby wadis likely supplemented water supply during peacetime.</value></Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>34.96053,31.98326,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Megiddo (תל מגידו)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Megiddo (תל מגידו)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Ancient City Water System</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jezreel Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5 (Pages 71)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>Despite massive city walls, an Early Bronze Age water system was likely present, possibly a depression in the northern part of the tel, though specific details are scarce due to later archaeological layers.</p>]]></description>
