      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Mizpon le-Fahma (תל מצפון לפחמה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Mizpon le-Fahma (תל מצפון לפחמה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 05. Early Bronze Age (EB) (-3300 to -2200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 3: Approximate Village / Spring Area (&lt; 500m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Samaria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.5.14 (Pages 67, 68)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (05. Early Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>This Early Bronze Age settlement, like others in Western Samaria, utilized unplastered cisterns carved into soft chalk bedrock to collect rainwater, compensating for the absence of nearby springs.</p>]]></description>
