      <Placemark>
        <name>Ebla (אבלה (סוריה))</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Ebla (אבלה (סוריה))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Syria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.12 (Pages 88, 89)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A very deep well in the lower city, connecting to a dome-roofed underground chamber, containing artifacts dated to around 2000 BCE.</p>]]></description>
