      <Placemark>
        <name>Jericho (יריחו)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Jericho (יריחו)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.3 (Pages 75)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>During the Middle Bronze Age, the city of Jericho was fortified, and Elisha&apos;s Spring (Ein es-Sultan) was intentionally included within its city walls to provide a secure water source.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Middle_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Jericho</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>יריחו</value></Data>
          <Data name="Era"><value>06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Spring Cave Capture</value></Data>
