        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Sha&apos;albim (שעלבים)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Sha&apos;albim (שעלבים)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.22 (Pages 92)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A burial cave from MB IIB was originally a rock-cut, mud-plastered water cistern, approximately 3m deep and 3m in diameter, with spiral steps for access.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Middle_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Sha&apos;albim</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>שעלבים</value></Data>
          <Data name="Era"><value>06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Plastered Cistern</value></Data>
          <Data name="Region"><value>Shephelah</value></Data>
          <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dates"><value>-2200 to -1550 BCE</value></Data>
          <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.6.22</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>92</value></Data>
          <Data name="Description"><value>A burial cave from MB IIB was originally a rock-cut, mud-plastered water cistern, approximately 3m deep and 3m in diameter, with spiral steps for access.</value></Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>34.98519,31.86333,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Dan (תל דן)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Dan (תל דן)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Upper Galilee</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.2 (Pages 73, 74, 75)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>The city of Dan, enclosed by a massive rampart, incorporated the eastern springs of Dan within its fortifications during the Middle Bronze Age, serving as the primary water source. An artificial water passage (sinkhole) was likely constructed concurrently with the rampart to manage excess water.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Middle_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Dan</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>תל דן</value></Data>
