      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Gerisa (תל גריסה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Gerisa (תל גריסה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Tunnel Shaft</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.6 (Pages 82, 83)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A water system consisting of an elliptical vertical shaft with steps, cut into the kurkar rock, was constructed during Middle Bronze Age IIA within the fortified city of Tel Gerisa to reach groundwater, likely for use during sieges.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Middle_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Gerisa</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>תל גריסה</value></Data>
