      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Lachish (תל לכיש)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Lachish (תל לכיש)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.10 (Pages 88)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A 44m deep, 2.4m diameter cylindrical well, stone-lined and rock-cut, located within the city&apos;s Middle Bronze Age fortifications and used until the Iron Age.</p>]]></description>
