      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Nami (תל נאמי)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Nami (תל נאמי)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.9 (Pages 87)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>An unfortified settlement featured a rectangular/oval well, 2.3m deep, lined with fieldstones, dated to MB IIA. Its bottom is 1.2m below current sea level, indicating a lower sea level in the MB period.</p>]]></description>
