        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>34.97173,31.74972,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Beth Shean (תל בית שאן)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Beth Shean (תל בית שאן)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 07. Late Bronze Age (LB) (-1550 to -1200 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.7.1 (Pages 98)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (07. Late Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A deep well, 13m deep and 0.86m in diameter, found in the southeastern part of Tel Beit She&apos;an. Its walls were built of bricks for 11.9m, with the rest being earlier fill. Dated to Stratum IXa (14th century BCE).</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Late_Bronze</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Beth Shean</value></Data>
