    <Folder>
      <name>08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</name>
      <description>תקופת הברזל 1 (Iron I) - 10 sites</description>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Ai (et-Tell) (העי (א-תל))</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Ai (et-Tell) (העי (א-תל))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.8 (Pages 113)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>Bell-shaped cisterns cut into the soft chalk rock, located beneath or near houses. One cistern was connected to two others, possibly for sedimentation, and was sealed when the house was abandoned around 3000 years ago (Iron Age I).</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_I</styleUrl>
