      <Placemark>
        <name>Khirbet Raddana (חורבת רדנה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Raddana (חורבת רדנה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.8 (Pages 113)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>Bell-shaped cisterns cut into the soft chalk rock, located beneath or near houses. These cisterns were crucial due to the distant and small local spring, providing sufficient water for the Iron Age I inhabitants.</p>]]></description>
