      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Beersheba (תל באר שבע)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Beersheba (תל באר שבע)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.4 (Pages 109, 110, 111)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>An ancient well located on the southeastern side of the tel. Its upper part is associated with the early layers (VI-IX) of Tel Beersheba, dating to Iron Age I (11th century BCE). The well is very deep, reaching 69m, and was likely connected to the earliest settlement.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_I</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Beersheba</value></Data>
