        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Beit Shemesh (תל בית שמש)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Beit Shemesh (תל בית שמש)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.3 (Pages 109)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>A large well, 3.3m in diameter, discovered north of the city gate. Its upper part is built with large stones. Mackenzie attributed it to the Philistine fortified city, dating its use to Iron Age I.</p>]]></description>
