      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Dor (תל דור)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Dor (תל דור)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.1 (Pages 107, 108)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>A rectangular well cut into kurkar rock, reaching the shallow water table. It underwent three construction phases, with pottery dating its use from the late 13th to early 11th century BCE (Iron Age I). It was built with ashlar stones and protected from sea waves.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_I</styleUrl>
