      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Gerisa (תל גריסה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Gerisa (תל גריסה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Deep Well</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Coastal Plain</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.2 (Pages 108, 109)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>An Iron Age I well built into an older Middle Bronze Age water system. It is a rectangular vertical shaft, constructed with large, roughly hewn stones, and its use is attributed to the Philistine settlement from the 11th century BCE.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_I</styleUrl>
