      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Hazor (תל חצור)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Hazor (תל חצור)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Aqueduct Channel</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Upper Galilee</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.11 (Pages 114)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>Two rock-cut aqueducts (northern and southern) were found west and southwest of the tel. They are unplastered and their early date is suggested by sherds in their fill, possibly dating to the Iron Age or even Early Bronze Age II.</p>]]></description>
