      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Taanach (תל תענך)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Taanach (תל תענך)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jezreel Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.6 (Pages 113)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>A cistern located beneath a courtyard of a building dated to the late 12th century BCE. It is 13.3m deep, with a built neck of 7m, and was fed by a plastered drainage channel from the courtyard.</p>]]></description>
