      <Placemark>
        <name>Tell es-Sa&apos;idiyeh (תל א-סעידיה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tell es-Sa&apos;idiyeh (תל א-סעידיה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 08. Iron Age I (-1200 to -1000 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.8.5 (Pages 111, 112)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (08. Iron Age I):</b></p>
<p>A monumental stepped water system with 95 preserved steps, leading down to a hidden spring. It was covered to conceal it from enemies. The system includes a small semi-circular pool and a plastered underground channel, dating its initial use to the mid-12th century BCE (Iron Age I).</p>]]></description>
