      <Placemark>
        <name>Baal-Meon (בעלמען)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Baal-Meon (בעלמען)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jordan</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.49 (Pages 183, 184)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>The Mesha Stele records King Mesha of Moab building the city of Baal-Meon and constructing a water reservoir (&apos;ashuah&apos;) or capturing a spring, possibly utilizing Israelite captives for their hydrological knowledge and labor.</p>]]></description>
