      <Placemark>
        <name>Horbat Rosh Zayit (חורבת ראש זית)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Horbat Rosh Zayit (חורבת ראש זית)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Lower Galilee</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.19 (Pages 160, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A rock-cut cistern found within the fortress, designed to collect rainwater runoff from the fortress area, dating to the 10th-9th centuries BCE. Cisterns or pools were found at Tel Ras ez-Zeit, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
