      <Placemark>
        <name>Horbat Shilha (חורבת שילחה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Horbat Shilha (חורבת שילחה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.24 (Pages 164, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A bell-shaped, rock-cut cistern (Locus 21) with a 0.85m opening and 1.8m diameter at 1.25m depth, located within a four-room house. Runoff was collected via earth channels. Plaster presence is not reported, but typical for such cisterns. Cisterns or pools were found at Shilha, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
