      <Placemark>
        <name>Kerem es-Samra (Kerem el-Ajez) (כרם א-סמרא (כרם אל עג&apos;ז))</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Kerem es-Samra (Kerem el-Ajez) (כרם א-סמרא (כרם אל עג&apos;ז))</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Reservoir</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Desert</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.30 (Pages 167)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>A large pool measuring 22x18m, located in the southwest of the fortress, with collapsed walls. It served as a water reservoir for the Iron Age II fortress.</p>]]></description>
