          <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>166, 167</value></Data>
          <Data name="Description"><value>The Abu Tabaq Cave, located at the foot of the fortress, served as a reservoir. It is 35m long, 7m wide, and 5m high, with a built entrance and steps leading inside. A rock-cut cistern, 18m from the Abu Tabaq Cave, approximately 6m deep with a 1m diameter opening. It is located beneath the fortress, suggesting a shaft for drawing water from within the fortification.</value></Data>
