        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Khirbet Meshura (חורבת משורה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.36 (Pages 171)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Three rock-cut cisterns, part of the Iron Age II water supply in the Negev Highlands, designed to store water.</p>]]></description>
