        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Beersheba (תל באר שבע)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Beersheba (תל באר שבע)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Ancient City Water System</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Negev</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.14, Summary (186) (Pages 153, 154, 155, 186, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>An elaborate internal city water system from Iron Age II, consisting of a deep entrance shaft, a large double-cruciform plastered reservoir (approx. 500 cubic meters) fed by floodwaters from Nahal Hebron via a channel, and a deep well outside the city walls (Iron Age I, but used in Iron Age II). Listed as one of 17 sites in Iron Age II Israel with a monumental water system, specifically mentioning a cruciform-shaped reservoir designed to maximize storage volume and prevent roof collapse. Wells were found at Tel Beersheba, including three associated with &apos;Nimrod&apos;, dating to the Iron Age II period. A reservoir with an external feeding system was identified at Tel Beersheba during the Iron Age II.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Beersheba</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>תל באר שבע</value></Data>
          <Data name="Era"><value>09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Ancient City Water System</value></Data>
          <Data name="Region"><value>Negev</value></Data>
          <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dates"><value>-1000 to -586 BCE</value></Data>
          <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.9.14, Summary (186)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>153, 154, 155, 186, 191</value></Data>
          <Data name="Description"><value>An elaborate internal city water system from Iron Age II, consisting of a deep entrance shaft, a large double-cruciform plastered reservoir (approx. 500 cubic meters) fed by floodwaters from Nahal Hebron via a channel, and a deep well outside the city walls (Iron Age I, but used in Iron Age II). Listed as one of 17 sites in Iron Age II Israel with a monumental water system, specifically mentioning a cruciform-shaped reservoir designed to maximize storage volume and prevent roof collapse. Wells were found at Tel Beersheba, including three associated with &apos;Nimrod&apos;, dating to the Iron Age II period. A reservoir with an external feeding system was identified at Tel Beersheba during the Iron Age II.</value></Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>34.83643,31.24566,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Beit Mirsim (תל בית מרסים)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Beit Mirsim (תל בית מרסים)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Shephelah</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.28 (Pages 165, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Several cisterns were found in Layer A (Iron Age II). One in the SE area (338-15) was 6m deep, with a built and rock-cut section, and a well-preserved, plastered channel leading to it from the NE, likely draining roofs. A settling basin was present at the channel&apos;s entry point. Cisterns or pools were found at Tel Beit Mirsim, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Site_Name"><value>Tel Beit Mirsim</value></Data>
          <Data name="Hebrew_Name"><value>תל בית מרסים</value></Data>
          <Data name="Era"><value>09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</value></Data>
          <Data name="Installation_Type"><value>Plastered Cistern</value></Data>
          <Data name="Region"><value>Shephelah</value></Data>
          <Data name="Location_Precision"><value>Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</value></Data>
