          <coordinates>34.97173,31.74972,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel en-Nasbeh (תל א-נצבה)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel en-Nasbeh (תל א-נצבה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Plastered Cistern</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Judean Hills</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.23 (Pages 162)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>The site contains numerous water cisterns, distinguished from granaries by their waterproof plaster, indicating their function for water storage during Iron Age II.</p>]]></description>
