      <Placemark>
        <name>Tel Taanach (תל תענך)</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Taanach (תל תענך)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 09. Iron Age II (-1000 to -586 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Tunnel Shaft</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jezreel Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.9.51 (Pages 185, 191)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (09. Iron Age II):</b></p>
<p>Mentioned as having an underground water system (from the Late Bronze Age) that provides a comparison for the type of system depicted in the Assyrian relief, implying its continued relevance or similar design in Iron Age II. Cisterns or pools were found at Tel Taanach, dated to the Iron Age II period.</p>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#style_Iron_Age_II</styleUrl>
