          <Data name="Chapter_Section"><value>2.9.40</value></Data>
          <Data name="Dissertation_Pages"><value>175, 176</value></Data>
          <Data name="Description"><value>The &apos;Mena&apos;s Canal&apos; (Manua&apos;s Canal), a 56 km long aqueduct built by King Manua (805-785 BCE), supplied water from the Engil river spring to Tushpa, overcoming the non-potable Lake Van water. It included stone dams, channels, and support walls up to 20m high, operating for 2500 years.</value></Data>
